font-size:15px\">You are challenged on what you know.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Common: </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">You a presented with information you are expected to already know.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Specific:</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> You fail a roll to make sense of information.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the look of these but could you elaborate on the Common one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T14:19:59-07:00","id":443115,"title":"","content":"Have you ever been lectured by someone without professional knowledge about your work? Like when a patient tells the doctor wich medicine she should be giving him? That's a Kuruth trigger if I've ever seen one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T22:31:13-07:00","id":443750,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Common: </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">You <u>are</u> presented with information you are expected to already know.</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> Well: An elder Wolf asks Joe Wolf a question regarding a spirit in Joe's turf Joe had never heard of before. Joe should be aware of Spirits on hist Turf, he is the Pack Spirit Shaman. This would be a Common Trigger.<br /> However: Joe Wolf is breaking into a lab, he finds he needs a pin to get through a door. He may not know the pin, but how can he be expected to know a pin he never used? If he was given the Pin prior to the job and he forgot the number than the situation would be a trigger.<br /> <br /> Thats what I had in mind. I think it should mention the info is uknown by the Wolf. so maybe t could be reworked as<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Common: </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">You are presented with <i>new</i> information you are expected to already know.</span></span></span></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T03:54:16-07:00","id":443991,"title":"","content":"Ah, that changes the Trigger a lot. I thought the trigger was due to being treated as dumb, like you need to be told something you of course know, wich is demeaning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T01:00:54-07:00","id":453956,"title":"","content":"I'm really at a loss for what to name this trigger, but it's based on the most common myths of what harms a Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <i>Passive: The touch of silver.</i><br /> <i>Common:The touch of moonstone (the semi-precious gem.)</i><br /> <i>Specific: The touch or ingestion of Wolfsbane (also called Monkshood or Devil's Helmet.)</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:40:29-07:00","id":454570,"title":"","content":"I haven't got common or passive, but my wolf's Specific trigger is a wolf who isn't pack pissing on her territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T11:34:39-07:00","id":454664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433833-some-new-kuruth-triggers?p=438855#post438855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having a tough time thinking of triggers for my character, the ST suggested I play a game or two to get into the character before deciding.<br /> <br /> However, I like the concept, and because I'm fond of this kind of thing I was thinking that if a Wolf-blooded had the <i>Devil Inside</i> Tell, after their first change they might develop triggers based upon it.<br /> <br /> <i>Passive</i>: Someone prays or calls to a religious power within earshot.<br /> <i>Common</i>: Someone brandishing a holy symbol or praying in order to ward off evil within earshot.<br /> <i>Specific</i>: Someone directing a holy symbol or prayer at you.<br /> <br /> I thought about adding a qualifier that it should excuse Uratha-oriented prayers that would be good for a more 'grounded' Uratha, but I kind of like the idea that they might cringe away from Luna or Father Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. I really like this one! Someone should compile a list!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T22:22:41-07:00","id":1214916,"title":"","content":"<b>Should Kuruth Triggers <i>evolve</i> with Uratha characters?</b> Question come to me when revisiting sheet of major NPC, part of the PCs pack, when checking her Triggers, as Auspice Moon is in the sky and group is in the middle of coffee shop in city center. As I did not wanted to make this scene about 'murderous friendly NPC', I changed her Triggers to new ones from Chris Allen's propositions in background.<br /> <br /> And there it hit me - Should Uratha evolve their Triggers with personal story? If yes, on what occasions? For this particular NPC I think about swapping two levels of Moon and Blood for one level level of Moon and two levels of Betrayal. Idea is that she was majory betrayed on previous pack on the night of her Auspice - and by this, her Death Rage. Now she is somehow callous and closet, even in interactions with her new pack - always suspecting betrayal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T22:54:27-07:00","id":1214925,"title":"","content":"Of course they should evolve, werewolves are creatures of change. It should likely involve some personal shift in the character or redefining moment. Like that betrayal leading to gaining the betrayed one seems fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-04-2018, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T05:40:36-07:00","id":1215005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xaielao</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433833-some-new-kuruth-triggers?p=453956#post453956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really at a loss for what to name this trigger, but it's based on the most common myths of what harms a Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <i>Passive: The touch of silver.</i><br /> <i>Common:The touch of moonstone (the semi-precious gem.)</i><br /> <i>Specific: The touch or ingestion of Wolfsbane (also called Monkshood or Devil's Helmet.)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Call it \u201cALLERGY\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T09:31:11-07:00","id":1218234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xaielao</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433833-some-new-kuruth-triggers?p=453956#post453956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really at a loss for what to name this trigger, but it's based on the most common myths of what harms a Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <i>Passive: The touch of silver.</i><br /> <i>Common:The touch of moonstone (the semi-precious gem.)</i><br /> <i>Specific: The touch or ingestion of Wolfsbane (also called Monkshood or Devil's Helmet.)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't touching silver already a general trigger? Or was it taking damage from silver?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Dam da namsithim.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","name":"Lost-His-Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T10:19:14-07:00","id":1218250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lost-His-Mind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433833-some-new-kuruth-triggers?p=1218234#post1218234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't touching silver already a general trigger? Or was it taking damage from silver?</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking damage from it. Requires it to be used as a weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T21:28:14-07:00","id":1218401,"title":"","content":"Mind if I try one? Based on an uncommon werewolf myth about their reflection always showing the wolf, even in human form.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Reflection</b></span><br /> Passive: You see your reflection.<br /> Common: You see your reflection clearly in a mirror or pool of water.<br /> Specific: You see your reflection in a mirror someone is brandishing towards you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":2598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","user":"Gryphon's Feather","date":". 09-10-2018, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T06:00:46-07:00","id":1218490,"title":"","content":"<s>This works best when paired with another character, though you could get amusing with it and make the target a sports team.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Rivalry</b></span><br /> Passive: You see your rival.<br /> Common: Your rival accomplishes something positive.<br /> Specific: Your rival surpasses you in way that negatively affects you.</s><br /> EDIT: A bit too similar to Envy, upon reflection.<br /> <br /> And this one, for the Werewolf who <i>really</i> likes their stuff<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Possessive</b></span><br /> Passive: Someone touches your things without permission.<br /> Common: Someone damages one of your possessions.<br /> Specific: Someone steals or destroys something you treasure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T06:29:14-07:00","id":1218502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433833-some-new-kuruth-triggers?p=1218490#post1218490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><s>This works best when paired with another character, though you could get amusing with it and make the target a sports team.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Rivalry</b></span><br /> Passive: You see your rival.<br /> Common: Your rival accomplishes something positive.<br /> Specific: Your rival surpasses you in way that negatively affects you.</s><br /> EDIT: A bit too similar to Envy, upon reflection.<br /> <br /> And this one, for the Werewolf who <i>really</i> likes their stuff<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Possessive</b></span><br /> Passive: Someone touches your things without permission.<br /> Common: Someone damages one of your possessions.<br /> Specific: Someone steals or destroys something you treasure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me. No one touches my stuff without permission","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T08:32:11-07:00","id":1218927,"title":"","content":"&lt;glances up at the MBTI posters&gt;<br /> <br /> <b>Competency</b><br /> <i>Passive: inability to agree on or set a goal.<br /> Common: Someone dismisses your logical decisions or ideas.<br /> Specific: Someone challenges your competence on a subject you have experience with.</i><br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T12:33:42-07:00","id":1219005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433833-some-new-kuruth-triggers?p=1218927#post1218927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;glances up at the MBTI posters&gt;<br /> <br /> <b>Competency</b><br /> <i>Passive: inability to agree on or set a goal.<br /> Common: Someone dismisses your logical decisions or ideas.<br /> Specific: Someone challenges your competence on a subject you have experience with.</i><br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh. Imagine being an Uratha in politics...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T13:35:10-07:00","id":1219031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433833-some-new-kuruth-triggers?p=1219005#post1219005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ugh. Imagine being an Uratha in politics...</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine being in a relationship....<br /> <br /> &quot;We have changed dinner and childcare plans six times in the last five minutes...! <i>I--I... urgh! Grr. GRRROWL! <b>Put your shoes on!! Get in the car--uurrhoowwwlll!!</b></i>&quot;<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf, who at least empathizes<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T17:51:52-07:00","id":1314616,"title":"","content":"Some new ones I've come up with, with their inspirations in parentheses.<br /> <br /> <b>Anthropocentric</b> (from the 1e flaw of the same name)<br /> <i>Passive</i>: You spend an hour outside hishu.<br /> <i>Common</i>: You spend a day outside hishu.<br /> <i>Specific</i>: You spend a week outside hishu.<br /> (For each these triggers, the character must spend at least an hour in hishu to reset the timer.)<br /> <br /> <b>Chance</b> (derived from a Geist 2e Crisis Point Trigger, examples given below)<br /> <i>Passive</i>: Be affected by a near-miss situation (e.g. almost hit by a car).<br /> <i>Common</i>: Suffer material harm from bad luck (injured by being hit by a car).<br /> <i>Specific</i>: Suffer serious material harm from bad luck (taking aggravated damage in a freak accident).<br /> <br /> <b>Changing</b> (as an opposite to Anthropocentric)<br /> <i>Passive</i>: You spend an hour without changing.<br /> <i>Common</i>: You spend a day in the same form.<br /> <i>Specific</i>: You spend a Lunar Phase in the same form.<br /> <br /> <b>Devil Inside </b>(from the Wolf-Blooded Tell, inspired by nofather's previous post)<br /> <i>Passive</i>: You are shown any religious iconography (like pamphlets).<br /> <i>Common</i>: You are shown key religious iconography (Cross, Star of David etc).<br /> <i>Specific</i>: You hold an item with prominent religious significance.<br /> <br /> <b>Helplessness </b>(Based on Geist 2e crisis point trigger)<br /> <i>Passive</i>: You are hurt (in any way) in a situation you cannot mitigate or control.<br /> <i>Common</i>: Dramatically fail a contested action.<br /> <i>Specific</i>: Watching a loved one die or be lost to you despite your efforts to save them.<br /> <br /> <b>Impatience</b> (common source of human anger)<br /> <i>Passive</i>: A task takes longer than expected.<br /> <i>Common</i>: You are involved in a task that takes longer than expected.<br /> <i>Specific</i>: Your schedule is deeply affected due to a task taking longer than expected.<br /> <br /> <b>Spite</b> (another from a Geist 2e crisis point trigger)<br /> <i>Passive</i>: Somebody deliberately attempts to hinder you.<br /> <i>Common</i>: A Social Merit is unavailable due to someone\u2019s deliberate attempt to block them.<br /> <i>Specific</i>: One of your Aspirations is thwarted by another\u2019s actions.<br /> <br /> <b>Touch</b> (probably needs better balancing)<br /> <i>Passive</i>: Being touched without your permission.<br /> <i>Common</i>: Being touched by a stranger without your permission.<br /> <i>Specific</i>: Being repeatedly touched without your permission.<br /> <br /> Hope you enjoy these!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":25357,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","user":"Lorekeeper","date":". 05-28-2019, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T06:04:11-07:00","id":1314695,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Denial</span></b><br /> <br /> Some Uratha cannot accept they are no longer human. While they understand their duty, they will try their best to think of themselves as sorcerors and mages rather than as werewolves.<br /> <br /> <i>Passive: </i>You have to rely on your animalistic side.<br /> <i>Common:</i> You have to change beyond Dalu.<br /> <i>Special:</i> You have to use Wolf Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 05-27-2019, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}